

One-time Jenkins setup

bash
sudo usermod -aG docker jenkins && sudo systemctl restart jenkins   # lets Jenkins run docker commands
sudo cp -r ~/.kube /var/lib/jenkins/ && sudo chown -R jenkins: /var/lib/jenkins/.kube   # kubectl access for Jenkins

With minikube, the certificate paths inside that kubeconfig must also be readable by the jenkins user. Copy ~/.minikube too and fix the paths. Jenkins also needs Git, a JDK and Docker installed.

Files in the GitHub repo

Hello.java: prints “Hello World”.


Dockerfile:
dockerfile
FROM eclipse-temurin:17-jdk
WORKDIR /app
COPY Hello.java .
RUN javac Hello.java
CMD ["java", "Hello"]

k8s.yaml:
yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata: {name: hello-java}
spec:
  replicas: 1
  selector: {matchLabels: {app: hello-java}}
  template:
    metadata: {labels: {app: hello-java}}
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: hello-java
        image: <dockerhub_user>/hello-java:v1
        command: ["sh","-c","java Hello && sleep 3600"]   # keeps the pod Running after it prints
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata: {name: hello-java-svc}
spec:
  selector: {app: hello-java}
  ports: [{port: 80, targetPort: 8080}]

Credentials (Q3): Manage Jenkins → Credentials → Global → Add Credentials → “Username with password”. Enter your Docker Hub username and password (or token), with ID dockerhub-creds.

Jenkinsfile. Create it via New Item → Pipeline → paste the script. For Q1, keep only the first three stages, then add the others as the questions progress.

groovy
pipeline {
  agent any
  environment { IMAGE = "<dockerhub_user>/hello-java" }
  stages {
    stage('Pull')    { steps { git branch: 'main', url: 'https://github.com/<user>/<repo>.git' } }   // Q1
    stage('Compile') { steps { sh 'javac Hello.java' } }
    stage('Run')     { steps { sh 'java Hello' } }
    stage('Docker Build') { steps { sh 'docker build -t $IMAGE:v1 .' } }       // Q2
    stage('Docker Run')   { steps { sh 'docker run --rm $IMAGE:v1' } }
    stage('Push') {                                                            // Q3
      steps {
        withCredentials([usernamePassword(credentialsId: 'dockerhub-creds', usernameVariable: 'U', passwordVariable: 'P')]) {
          sh 'echo $P | docker login -u $U --password-stdin'   // login without exposing the password
          sh 'docker push $IMAGE:v1'
        }
      }
    }
    stage('Deploy') {                                                          // Q4
      steps {
        sh 'kubectl apply -f k8s.yaml'      // the cluster pulls the image from Docker Hub
        sh 'kubectl get pods'
      }
    }
  }
}

Click Build Now, open the build, and check Console Output. For DockerHub, open the repo page. For Kubernetes, kubectl get pods should show Running.
